# Source-distribution contents (issue #264).
#
# Without this file the sdist is whatever setuptools guesses, which for
# this repository was wrong in both directions: with a git file-finder in
# the build environment it swept in every tracked file — including
# `figures/`, ~17.6 MB of rendered PNGs (two 8.4 MB page figures alone) —
# and without one it silently dropped `docs/`, the `tests/` subpackages
# and the project metadata files. Both failure modes are now spelled out
# below, and the `sdist contents` guard in ci.yml / release.yml fails the
# build if an excluded path ever reappears in the tarball.
#
# Choice of scope: the sdist ships the sources needed to build, test and
# document the package from the tarball alone (src, tests, docs, runnable
# examples and validation drivers) — the norm for a scientific package
# whose users are expected to re-run its verification. What it does NOT
# ship is anything *rendered*: figures, validation plots/CSVs and built
# docs are regenerable outputs, they dominate the archive size, and PyPI
# is not an image host. The wheel is unaffected either way: it is built
# from the src-layout package and never contained these paths.

# --- Project metadata beyond the defaults (README/LICENSE/pyproject) ---
include CHANGELOG.md
include CITATION.cff
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include requirements.txt
include requirements-test.txt

# --- Sources shipped in the sdist ---
graft src
graft tests
graft docs
graft examples
graft validation

# --- Rendered outputs and repo-only tooling: never in the sdist ---
prune figures
prune docs/_build
prune .github
prune .claude
prune .streamlit
recursive-exclude validation *.png *.csv *.json *.inp *.vtk
recursive-exclude examples *.png *.json *.inp *.vtk

# --- Caches and editor droppings ---
global-exclude *.py[cod] *.so .DS_Store
global-exclude __pycache__/*
prune .benchmarks
prune .pytest_cache
prune .ruff_cache
prune .mypy_cache
